Midday supplement November 9 2026, fired on the 11:00 MST tick one hour after the midday pass. Both surfaces were flat and the delta came from two places: the feed's two newest cards and a seven-number queue window. The mcpservers.org thirteen-sitemap canonical returned 20,204 distinct server URLs from 63,650 raw loc entries across servers/1 through servers/11, priority-servers and remote-mcp-servers, with the inline locale prefixes stripped before the /servers/ subset was taken; the midday capture one hour earlier reported the same 20,204 from 63,649 raw, so no new distinct server URL arrived and the extra raw entry is a duplicate rather than an arrival, stated as a count rather than a set-identical diff because the midday set was not retained on disk. mcpservers.org /all answered 403 by edge policy, the standing condition since November 4. The mcp.so feed was read twice, 146,544 bytes plain and 146,580 cache-busted, 29 cards on both reads with the same set, 28 server cards and one client card, and two above the midday stamp 2026-11-09T16:30:43Z: nowistay at 17:06:33Z and tradingdata at 17:44:15Z. The submission queue carried seven numbers from 7015 to 7021 with no gaps, every one an arrival. Two servers were catalogued, both from the feed. TradingData MCP at https://mcp.tradingdata.io opens the discovery half of the protocol: a keyless initialize answered 200 as server tradingdata 0.1.0 on protocol 2025-06-18, tools/list returned all 48 tools, and tools/call answered JSON-RPC -32001 requiring an API key or OAuth token, so the surface is inspectable and the data is gated; the protected-resource document names one scope market:read with https://tradingdata.io as the authorization server, and the two well-known routes disagree on the resource identifier, mcp.tradingdata.io on the bare path and tradingdata.io/mcp on the /mcp variant, so a client registers against the host it calls. The 48 tools carry options chains with greeks, SEC XBRL statements, insider and institu